# The posture checks known to fail on every form (make check;
# test/console.zig, test/cage):
#
#   * ID...      on any form built as it ships
#   ARCH ID...   on that architecture (x86_64, aarch64)
#
# A form takes the * line, the ARCH line, and the weaknesses its own
# form.yaml names, each with its excuse (forms/README.md). ?ID may fail or
# not, as the host decides. Each is a weakness still open
# (docs/security.md, "Not yet"): the console fails a machine on any other
# failure, and on any of these that starts passing, so no list can claim
# less, or more, than the machines hold.
#
# No form carries a shell but those that log people in (sshd, lima,
# prod-ssh). make check-dist boots prod-ssh's release disk as it ships:
# busybox for the logins sshd serves, and sshd listening.
#
# The boot chain is not verified end to end yet (docs/design/
# verified-boot.md): Secure Boot is off (?boot-secure-boot: it is on
# wherever the firmware takes the key), only protected images load an IPE
# release policy (boot-ipe-enforced), and no TPM counter guards the slot
# serial (boot-rollback-protected). Phase 4 and phase 5 close these.

* ?boot-secure-boot boot-rollback-protected boot-ipe-enforced
